T {[S] start-up} 125 -1090 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {m = 8: Q2 = 8 x Q1} 565 -160 0 0 0.25 0.25 {}
T {[R] output, I_ref} 825 -1090 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[C] bandgap core} 365 -1090 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] PMOS diodes, NMOS sinks} 1385 -1090 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] vabp} 1225 -1090 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] PMOS sources, NMOS diodes} 1865 -1090 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] vabn} 1705 -1090 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {d2s_bias_bg_pd: self-contained bias, current-mode bandgap with pnpMPA and rhigh + mirror tree of d2s_bias_in, digital enable en_3v3} 60 -1290 0 0 0.5 0.5 {}
T {branch current V_BE1/R1 + U_T ln 8 / R0 = 2.5 uA; I_ref = 2 x branch = 5 uA into NI (through TGN / TGP); Q1 / Q2: emitter 2u x 2u} 60 -1240 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {bg_core: current-mode (Banba type) bandgap, no op-amp.} 60 -20 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   The PMOS mirror makes both branch currents equal and the NMOS pair NA / NB (gates on g) forces ea = eb, so each} 60 4 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   branch carries V_BE1 / R1 + U_T ln 8 / R0 (Q2 = 8 x Q1). rhigh (-0.22 %/K) nearly cancels V_BE's -1.77 mV/K already,} 60 28 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   so the PTAT share through R0 is small. PO / POC deliver twice the branch current, 5 uA, into NI.} 60 52 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   R1A is 10 % longer than R1B: with both PNPs off the loop gain is then > 1, so the core cannot rest there.} 60 76 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   PB / PBC are stacked diodes; the PMOS run in moderate inversion for headroom at 3.0 V, ss, -40 C.} 60 100 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {Mirror tree and diodes. The six diodes are those of d2s_bias_lp and set the bias voltages:} 60 124 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   vbp: BP 5u/6u, 5 uA (unit tails).  vbpc: BPC 1u/4u, 2 uA (mirror cascodes).  vabp: RP2 on RP1, 5 uA (ABP, FPL).} 60 148 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   vbn: BN 6u/6u, 5 uA (fold sinks).  vbnc: BNC 1u/8u, 2 uA (fold cascodes).  vabn: RN2 on RN1, 5 uA (ABN, FNL).} 60 172 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {PMOS gate lines come from PMOS diodes on vdd, NMOS gate lines from NMOS diodes on vss: bias crosses blocks as currents.} 60 196 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {RP1 and RN1 are the class-AB replicas of OP and ON: they sit on the output-stage rails vddo / vsso (separate rails} 60 220 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   from the right). RP2 keeps its n-well on vdd, like ABP. RN1 needs a local substrate tap ring on vsso, like ON.} 60 244 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
